utional features", "Myelodysplastic syndrome (MDS-EB): possible but requires bone marrow analysis to confirm", "Reactive lymphocytosis from chronic illness: inconsistent with blast count and systemic symptoms", "De Novo Acute Myeloid Leukemia (AML): dangerous alternative with posterior 0.31 despite current evidence favoring MDS-EB"], "alarm_features": ["weight loss", "night sweats", "fever", "pancytopenia with blasts"]}, "branches": {"B1": {"id": "B1", "label": "Myeloid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "live", "prior": 0.3794704351059874, "posterior": 0.3794704351059874, "danger": 0.9, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.0, "evidence_for": [], "evidence_against": [], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": [], "closure_reason": "", "turn_cost_to_refine": 2.0, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.8, "interrupt_relevance": 0.9, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "mechanism", "representative_diseases": []}, "B2": {"id": "B2", "label": "Lymphoid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "live", "prior": 0.34172740795834883, "posterior": 0.34172740795834883, "danger": 0.85, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.0, "evidence_for": [], "evidence_against": [], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": [], "closure_reason": "", "turn_cost_to_refine": 1.5, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.75, "interrupt_relevance": 0.8, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "mechanism", "representative_diseases": []}, "B3": {"id": "B3", "label": "Chronic Myeloproliferative Neoplasm (chronic/accelerated phase)", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "live", "prior": 0.0346827817032354, "posterior": 0.0346827817032354, "danger": 0.7, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.0, "evidence_for": [], "evidence_against": [], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": [], "closure_reason": "", "turn_cost_to_refine": 1.2, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.65, "interrupt_relevance": 0.6, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "mechanism", "representative_diseases": []}, "B4": {"id": "B4", "label": "Lymphoproliferative / Plasma Cell Disorder", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "live", "prior": 0.05649683897359612, "posterior": 0.05649683897359612, "danger": 0.6, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.0, "evidence_for": [], "evidence_against": [], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": [], "closure_reason": "", "turn_cost_to_refine": 2.0, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.6, "interrupt_relevance": 0.5, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "mechanism", "representative_diseases": []}, "B5": {"id": "B5", "label": "Reactive / Non-malignant Leukocytosis", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "live", "prior": 0.03162253625883228, "posterior": 0.03162253625883228, "danger": 0.3, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.0, "evidence_for": [], "evidence_against": [], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": [], "closure_reason": "", "turn_cost_to_refine": 1.0, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.5, "interrupt_relevance": 0.2, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "mechanism", "representative_diseases": []}}, "frontier": ["B1", "B2", "B3", "B4", "B5"], "other_mass": 0.0, "pending_results": [], "actions_taken": [{"t": 2, "type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Does the high blast count (35%) in peripheral blood and subacute onset (days to weeks) argue against CML in blast crisis due to its typically lower blast percentages and chronic progression?", "summary": "CML in blast crisis typically presents with lower blast percentages and chronic progression, strongly reducing its likelihood."}, {"t": 2, "type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Does the combination of pancytopenia (anemia, thrombocytopenia) and 35% blasts in peripheral blood suggest MDS-EB rather than de novo AML?", "summary": "The combination is more indicative of MDS-EB than de novo AML, moderately supporting MDS-EB while weakly reducing AML support."}, {"t": 2, "type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Do the visual symptoms (blurry vision, reduced acuity) and lack of lymphadenopathy in the vignette contradict de novo B-cell ALL?", "summary": "Visual symptoms are uncommon in ALL, while absent lymphadenopathy reduces likelihood, resulting in weak reduction for B-cell ALL."}, {"t": 2, "type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Does the absence of documented prior CLL diagnosis or chronic lymphocytosis in the vignette strongly argue against CLL in blast crisis?", "summary": "Lack of documented chronic lymphocytosis strongly reduces likelihood of CLL in blast crisis."}, {"t": 2, "type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Does the absence of lymphoma-specific findings (e.g., lymphadenopathy, organomegaly) in the vignette argue against lymphoma with leukemic phase as the diagnosis?", "summary": "Lymphadenopathy and organomegaly are typical in lymphoma; their absence weakly argues against this diagnosis."}, {"t": 2, "type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Does the high blast percentage (35%) and lack of chronic phase features (e.g., lymphocytosis) in peripheral blood make CLL in blast crisis less likely than de novo ALL?", "summary": "The high blast percentage without chronic phase features strongly argues against CLL in blast crisis but only weakly affects ALL."}], "differential_history": [{"top": [["B1", 0.372], ["B2", 0.335], ["B2.1", 0.234]]}, {"top": [["B1", 0.31], ["B1.1", 0.298], ["B2", 0.082]]}], "deliberation": {}, "interrupt": {"active": false, "reason": "No acute life-threatening instability markers identified (airway, respiratory, or haemodynamic compromise). Time-critical conditions like septic shock, meningitis, or tension pneumothorax are not indicated by current findings.", "required_actions": []}, "termination": {"ready_to_stop": false, "termination_type": "confirmation", "reason": "Root posterior (0.75) meets threshold but dangerous alternative B1 (AML, posterior 0.31, danger 0.9) remains unresolved."}, "turn_budget_used": 2, "estimated_remaining_value": 0.5, "max_turn_budget": 5, "latest_action_type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "diagnosis_readiness_score": 0.2983973987198761, "benchmark_output_ready": false, "static_question": "Which of the following is the most likely diagnosis?", "static_options": [{"id": "A", "description": "Acute lymphoblastic leukemia"}, {"id": "B", "description": "Acute myelogenous leukemia"}, {"id": "C", "description": "Chronic lymphocytic leukemia"}, {"id": "D", "description": "Chronic myelogenous leukemia"}, {"id": "E", "description": "Multiple myeloma"}], "seen_evidence_ids": [], "seen_evidence_phenotypes": "{'Bence Jones Proteinuria', 'Multiple myeloma', 'lymphocytosis', 'elevated white blood cell count', 'elevated red blood cell count', 'blood'}", "mode_policy": {"benchmark_purity": true, "allow_external_knowledge": true}, "answer_option_mapping": {}, "tool_use_log": [], "root_revision_needed": false, "max_tree_depth": 3, "reasoning_ledger": {"anchor": {"hypothesis": "B1", "t": 0, "posterior_at_anchor": 0.372}, "leader": {"branch_id": "B1", "label": "Myeloid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts", "posterior": 0.379, "leading_since_t": 0, "n_revisions": 0}, "leader_evidence": {"confirming": 0, "disconfirming": 0, "last_disconfirming_digest": ""}, "action_intents": [{"t": 2, "intent": "broaden"}, {"t": 2, "intent": "broaden"}, {"t": 2, "intent": "broaden"}, {"t": 2, "intent": "broaden"}, {"t": 2, "intent": "broaden"}, {"t": 2, "intent": "broaden"}], "considered_alternatives": ["B2", "B4"]}, "discriminator_hints": "[Knowledge Layer: coverage=60%, source=primekg]\n\nMyeloid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts vs Lymphoid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts:\n  Favours first:  abnormality of the bladder, abnormality of vitamin b12 metabolism, acute kidney injury, bone pain, decreased circulating antibody level\n  Favours second: abnormality of skin physiology, abnormality of the endocrine system, acrocyanosis, areflexia, arterial thrombosis\n\nMyeloid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts vs Chronic Myeloproliferative Neoplasm (chronic/accelerated phase):\n  Favours first:  abnormality of the bladder, abnormality of vitamin b12 metabolism, acute kidney injury, bone pain, elevated serum creatinine\n  Favours second: abnormal bronchus physiology, abnormal cd4:cd8 ratio, absent speech, agammaglobulinemia, anorexia\n\nLymphoid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts vs Chronic Myeloproliferative Neoplasm (chronic/accelerated phase):\n  Favours first:  abnormality of skin physiology, abnormality of the endocrine system, acrocyanosis, areflexia, arterial thrombosis\n  Favours second: abnormal bronchus physiology, abnormal cd4:cd8 ratio, absent speech, agammaglobulinemia, anorexia\n\nRelated to Myeloid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts: cd4+/cd56+ hematodermic neoplasm, hematopoietic and lymphoid cell neoplasm, mast cell neoplasm\n\nRelated to Lymphoid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts: hematopoietic and lymphoid cell neoplasm, lymphoid leukemia (disease), lymphoma\n\nRelated to Chronic Myeloproliferative Neoplasm (chronic/accelerated phase): bone marrow cancer, chronic eosinophilic leukemia, chronic eosinophilic leukemia, not otherwise specified\n\n[Indirect reasoning chains (PrimeKG 2-hop):]\n  and night sweats → fatigue → Myeloid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts\n  and night sweats → pain → Lymphoid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts\n  and night sweats → fatigue → Lymphoid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts"}
